// dependencies.dot - GENERATED from evidence.json by gen_dot.py; do not hand-edit.
// Gate: verify_refs.py (resolves every citation against the real files),
//      cross_check.py (this file must agree with evidence.json and the DSL).
// Question this graph answers: what does each part of DesktopIconToggle.exe depend on,
//      and which of those edges leave the process?
// Reading order: cluster In-process components -> edge colour. Red = crosses into explorer's
//      process. Green = a guard/timer that exists to protect the 300 ms hook timeout.
//      Dashed = not an ordinary call (async, broadcast, or a read-only diagnostic).
// Edge labels carry the evidence.json edge id, then the relationship type, then the citations,
//      so any claim in this graph is checkable without opening the JSON.
digraph DesktopIconToggle_Dependencies {
  rankdir=TB;
  graph [fontname="Segoe UI", fontsize=10, nodesep=0.42, ranksep=1.05,
         compound=true, labelloc=t, pagesize="", dpi=110,
